Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:01:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rewrite the Websites pillar copy and drop Framer

"Websites that get found and get bookings." -> "Fast, stunning websites
that show off your business." Changed in both places it appears: the
Websites card in What We Do on Home, and the /websites hero. A full stop
was added to match the other three pillar headings, which all carry one.

Framer is gone from the shipped site. It appeared twice:

- The Home one-liner named it as a build platform. Rewritten as "custom
  coded or on your platform of choice, Shopify, WordPress and more". Also
  drops the "Custom-designed ... custom coded" repetition the direct
  substitution would have created.
- The /websites platform strip listed it as a chip. Removed, and the strip
  is relabelled from "Platforms we build on" to "Custom coded, or on your
  platform of choice", so the section leads with custom build rather than
  reading as a list of page builders.

Two things deliberately left alone:

- The /websites meta title still reads "Websites that get found and get
  bookings". It is a title tag on a domain that migrated yesterday, and
  changing indexed title copy is a search decision rather than a copy one.
  Every visible instance is updated; this is the only survivor.
- mockups/home.html still carries the old headline and one-liner. It is the
  approved visual spec, a record of what was signed off, not shipped code.

Verified on a production build: both pages render the new headline, no
occurrence of "Framer" remains anywhere in content/, src/ or public/, and
the one-liner and platform strip render as intended.

